    "title": "New endowment, matching gifts to boost resources for WCU track, field, cross country - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Via catamountsports.com, ,\n1 days ago Bill Studenc September 25, 2026 A new endowment established by a competitive racewalker from Whittier is designed to help the Western Carolina University track and field and cross country programs overcome hurdles, with a campaign for matching gifts in the starting blocks to help push the effort across the finish line. Created through a $100,000 commitment from retired physical therapist Andrew Smith and wife LouAnn, the endowment will result in financial support for WCU’s cross country and track and field programs. The specific purpose of the Andrew “Andy” L. and LouAnn M. Smith Track and Field Support Endowment is to… Read full article",
    "summary": "1 days ago Bill Studenc September 25, 2026 A new endowment established by a competitive racewalker from Whittier is designed to help the Western Carolina University track and field and cross country programs overcome hurdles, with a campaign for matching gifts in the starting blocks to help push the effort across the finish line. Created through a $100,000 commitment from retired physical therapist Andrew Smith and wife LouAnn, the endowment will result in financial support for WCU’s cross country and track and field programs.",
